{"resource":{"id":"ka-P7rIoNsqfsQ","title":"Convertir des degrés en radians","s":"maths","t":"","p":"khan","f":"video","c":"Algèbre III","u":"Trigonométrie","d":422,"l":"progressive","v":"P7rIoNsqfsQ","url":"https://fr.khanacademy.org/math/be-4eme-secondaire2/x213a6fc6f6c9e122:trigonometrie/x213a6fc6f6c9e122:hors-programme-cercle-trigonometrique-et-radians/v/we-converting-degrees-to-radians","b":0},"descriptionHtml":"Pour convertir des degrés en radians, il faut multiplier le nombre de degrés par &pi;/180. On obtient la mesure d'un angle en radians. Par exemple,  90 degrés=90 &pi;/180= &pi;/2 radians.","related":[{"id":"ka-nRXLEqk09Vs","title":"Conversions entre degrés et radians","f":"video"},{"id":"ka-iKH_arXfyHI","title":"Convertir des radians en degrés","f":"video"},{"id":"ka-YOnyX-kG2pQ","title":"Angles en radians et quadrants","f":"video"}],"attribution":"Khan Academy et ses contributeurs","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","sourceUrl":"https://fr.khanacademy.org/math/be-4eme-secondaire2/x213a6fc6f6c9e122:trigonometrie/x213a6fc6f6c9e122:hors-programme-cercle-trigonometrique-et-radians/v/we-converting-degrees-to-radians"}